From 547873303537b10565935270c11061cec534f36f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Casado <mcasado80@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 04:47:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Restructure as a monorepo; retire agent-duo-codex

Protocol docs, prompt templates, and duo.sh existed in two repos and had to be
kept byte-identical by hand. Drift between them fails at runtime as a silent
stall, which is the worst way to find out, and the duplication was growing
rather than shrinking.

Single source of truth per file:
  references/  protocol, orchestration mapping, Orca notes
  prompts/     the four templates
  bin/duo.sh   the one launcher

claude/SKILL.md and codex/AGENTS.md remain separate because the two agents read
instructions from different places, but both now point at the same sources.
build.sh assembles dist/agent-duo.skill; dist/ is generated and gitignored.

Also removes launch.sh and launch-orca.sh: duo.sh does the same job in fewer
steps, and three launchers is three things to keep in sync.
